  "worked_solution": "The graph $y={x}^{12}$ looks similar to an upward parabola, so\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }{x}^{12}=\\infty .\n$$\n\nMultiplication by the positive constant $8$ does not affect the limit at infinity. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }(8{x}^{12})={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }({x}^{12})=\\infty .\\end{aligned}\n$$",
